{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The trusted run observed a complete mismatch: node 2’s request was admitted and confirmed as `301:101`, but its delivered response and exported readiness carried node 3’s context, `302:202`. Node 3 retained its own context. Both requests left the leader’s pending queue, and all held messages were released.\n\nI’m recording this as a Peer-level identity-preservation defect. The run did not measure a client timeout, stale application read, or broader liveness failure.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='b3582539d580412caa5467e8fc2f56c5',rationale='Review the fixed first-version check against C-read-context version 1 and its actual trusted execution. A complete per-origin context mismatch is observed; scope remains Peer readiness identity, not client liveness or application linearizability.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S-context-contract','S-read-context-test','S-prefix-context-test','S-read-queue','S-read-response','S-follower-read','S-client-batches','S-peer-launch','S-bootstrap','S-peer-update','S-peer-export','S-peer-members','S-memory-db','S-logdb-interface','S-peer-admission','S-message-term','S-read-send','S-replication-recv','S-ticks','S-engine-order','S-node-effects'],rationale='The fixed plan and harness match C-read-context v1: preservation of the SystemCtx identifying each successfully confirmed remote operation. S-context-contract explicitly defines SystemCtx as operation identity; S-read-context-test checks remote readiness against the initiating context; S-prefix-context-test preserves each returned earlier status context. These support the equality oracle independently of the suspect emitter. This is not an eventual-success assertion. The driver uses Launch and three distinct bootstrap addresses, processes real bootstrap entries and the elected no-op, persists each update into the existing TestLogDB before delivery, and acknowledges updates through Commit and NotifyRaftLastApplied. It sets no private raft fields and overrides no handler. Only memory persistence, synchronous application of bootstrap/no-op entries, clock scheduling, fixed opaque contexts and transport scheduling are substituted. No crash, later membership change or application command occurs. Election happens via Tick and actual votes, and the setup guard witnesses a leader with current-term committed entry plus common applied prefix. The recorded setup was leader 1, term 2, commit 4. Every delivered message is an actual Peer output, with Peer.Handle retaining membership and term checks. Earlier-context heartbeat replies are held while the later request is admitted; this preserves the investigated overlap. Afterward all held replies are delivered, independent of comparison outcome. Prefix-confirmation events observe live registered status pointers removed by the same-term heartbeat handler, retain each status context and index, and precede result events. There is no intervening role change or other pending-state reset in the read phase; removal is attributable to readIndex.confirm. The fixed monitor uses admission_alias=confirmed, with declared references to admitted context/term. It correlates by scenario and origin, independently of the compared context; exactly one request exists per origin and duplicate origins abort setup. Execution b5f3cb2c346040a9b22ca064ee24a691 admits origin 2 as 301:101 and origin 3 as 302:202. An actual reply from voter 2 for 302:202 confirms both statuses at index 4 in term 2. The response delivered to origin 2 and its GetUpdate ReadyToReads copy both contain 302:202; origin 3 also contains 302:202, correctly for its own request. Monitor witness 6 therefore differs from admitted event 1 after confirmed event 3; the independent origin 3 comparison uses events 2, 4 and 8. Parsing reports no errors and both comparisons are complete. Readiness is copied directly from the target Update before Commit clears it, so the mismatch is an exported protocol result, not a fabricated client cache value. The matching wire response corroborates the source branch that uses triggering m.Hint/m.HintHigh instead of each s.ctx. End diagnostics show two admitted operations, zero pending reads, zero queued and zero held messages. Process PASS establishes only completed harness execution; the property monitor separately reports violated. No concrete correspondence issue was found in this scope.',counterevidence=['The latest remote request retains its correct context; local-origin statuses use s.ctx correctly in source. The defect is conditional on a confirmed prefix containing an earlier distinct remote context.','The client API permits timeout outcomes and pendingReadIndex requires exact context; neither establishes a client deadline violation in this Peer-only execution.','All compared read indexes are 4 with applied index 4; no stale value or index regression is demonstrated.'],limitations=['Real transport, NodeHost pending-batch machinery and an application state machine are not executed; client timeout is a potential consequence inferred from exact-key consumption, not an observed endpoint.','TestLogDB is memory-backed and no crash occurs. Durability, recovery, configuration changes, context collisions and other schedules remain outside the claim.','Queue removal is treated as successful confirmation only in this fixed same-term read-only message phase, where source and actual messages exclude reset/removal alternatives.','No claim of infinite stalling, numeric deadline violation or whole-cluster linearizability failure.'],report_title='远端 ReadIndex 批量确认替换了较早请求的标识',report_answer='三节点、固定任期与成员配置下，节点 2 的请求以 301:101 注册并获确认，但其收到的响应及 ReadyToRead 均为节点 3 的 302:202。检查验证的是 Peer 层操作标识传播错误；未执行客户端超时或应用层陈旧读。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['a118363ef443443ca4bcfe8f5be0f751','b3582539d580412caa5467e8fc2f56c5','b5f3cb2c346040a9b22ca064ee24a691','B-read-confirm','B-read-deliver','S-read-response','S-read-queue','S-context-contract'],answered='Trusted execution observed the earlier remote request identity replaced by the later confirming context in both delivered response and originating Peer readiness, despite actual successful confirmation retaining the earlier status identity. The same-history latest request retained its own context. The fixed monitor comparison is complete and this review finds no concrete correspondence issue for C-read-context v1.',remaining=['Actual NodeHost client timeout and application-read consequences were not measured.','Other legal membership-transition and authority histories remain independent investigation questions.'],understanding='updated',rationale='This answers the selected per-operation identity propagation proposition. Source identifies remote response field selection as the cause; broader progress or safety claims are not licensed.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission4.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_18-11-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission4.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
